<title>UK: BOE gives UK money market 50 mln stg further help.</title>
<headline>BOE gives UK money market 50 mln stg further help.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said it provided the UK money market with a further 50 million stg of assistance at established interest rates.</p>
<p>			    EARLY	1200 GMT   1400 GMT   LATE</p>
<p> FORECAST SHORTAGE    400 MLN    400 MLN    250 MLN    =</p>
<p> CUMULATIVE SUPPLY    =	    150 MLN    200 MLN    =</p>
<p>DETAILS</p>
<p> BAND 1  BANK BILLS   =	    150 MLN*   50  MLN*   =</p>
<p>* INTEREST RATE - 5-15/16 PCT (INDICATES UNCHANGED BASE RATES)</p>
</text>
